            Encapsulates HTTP method, path, headers, query string, and body\\n  
            - Easy access to form data and query parameters\\n   - Automatic    
            parsing of request data\\n\\n3. **Response Object**\\n   -          
            Configurable status codes, headers, and body content\\n   - Support 
            for different content types\\n   - WSGI-compatible response         
            handling\\n\\n4. **Jinja2 Template Rendering**\\n   - Integrated    
            template engine with application context\\n   - Support for template
            inheritance and includes\\n   - Automatic HTML escaping for         
            security\\n\\n5. **Application Context Management**\\n   -          
            Thread-local storage for `current_app` and `g` objects\\n   -       
            Context-aware request handling\\n   - Safe concurrent request       
            processing\\n\\n6. **Blueprint-based Modular Applications**\\n   -  
            Organize routes and handlers into reusable blueprints\\n   - URL    
            prefix inheritance for blueprint registration\\n   - Modular        
            application architecture\\n\\n## Installation\\n\\n```bash\\npip    
            install -e .\\n```\\n\\n## Quick Start\\n\\n### Basic               
            Application\\n\\n```python\\nfrom flaskframework import Flask,      
            render_template\\n\\napp =                                          
            Flask(__name__)\\n\\n@app.route(\'/\')\\ndef hello():\\n    return  
            \'Hello, World!\'\\n\\n@app.route(\'/user/<name>\')\\ndef           
            user_profile(name):\\n    return f\'Hello,                          
            {name}!\'\\n\\n@app.route(\'/user/<int:id>\')\\ndef                 
            user_by_id(id):\\n    return f\'User ID: {id}\'\\n\\nif __name__ == 
            \'__main__\':\\n    app.run(debug=True)\\n```\\n\\n### Using        
            Templates\\n\\nCreate a `templates/` directory and add              
            `hello.html`:\\n\\n```html\\n<!DOCTYPE html>\\n<html>\\n<head>\\n   
            <title>Hello {{ name }}</title>\\n</head>\\n<body>\\n    <h1>Hello, 
            {{ name }}!</h1>\\n</body>\\n</html>\\n```\\n\\n```python\\nfrom    
            flaskframework import Flask, render_template\\n\\napp =             
            Flask(__name__)\\n\\n@app.route(\'/hello/<name>\')\\ndef            
            hello(name):\\n    return render_template(\'hello.html\',           
            name=name)\\n\\nif __name__ == \'__main__\':\\n                     
            app.run()\\n```\\n\\n### Using Blueprints\\n\\n```python\\nfrom     
            flaskframework import Flask, Blueprint\\n\\n# Create a              
            blueprint\\napi = Blueprint(\'api\', __name__,                      
            url_prefix=\'/api\')\\n\\n@api.route(\'/users\')\\ndef              
            list_users():\\n    return {\'users\': [\'alice\',                  
            \'bob\']}\\n\\n@api.route(\'/users/<int:id>\')\\ndef                
            get_user(id):\\n    return {\'user_id\': id}\\n\\n# Create the main 
            app\\napp =                                                         
            Flask(__name__)\\napp.register_blueprint(api)\\n\\n@app.route(\'/\')
            \\ndef index():\\n    return \'Main application\'\\n\\nif __name__  
            == \'__main__\':\\n    app.run()\\n```\\n\\n### Application         
            Context\\n\\n```python\\nfrom flaskframework import Flask,          
            current_app, g\\n\\napp =                                           
            Flask(__name__)\\n\\n@app.before_request\\ndef before_request():\\n 
            g.user = \'anonymous\'\\n\\n@app.route(\'/context\')\\ndef          
            show_context():\\n    return f\'App: {current_app.import_name},     
            User: {g.user}\'\\n\\nif __name__ == \'__main__\':\\n               
            app.run()\\n```\\n\\n## API Reference\\n\\n### Flask                
            Application\\n\\n#### `Flask(import_name,                           
            template_folder=\'templates\')`\\n\\nCreate a new Flask             
            application.\\n\\n- `import_name`: The name of the application      
            package\\n- `template_folder`: Directory containing Jinja2          
            templates\\n\\n#### Methods\\n\\n- `route(rule, methods=None,       
            endpoint=None)`: Decorator for adding routes\\n- `add_url_rule(rule,
            endpoint, view_func, methods=None)`: Add URL rule                   
            programmatically\\n- `register_blueprint(blueprint, **options)`:    
            Register a blueprint\\n- `errorhandler(code)`: Decorator for error  
            handlers\\n- `before_request(f)`: Decorator for before-request      
            handlers\\n- `after_request(f)`: Decorator for after-request        
            handlers\\n- `run(host=\'127.0.0.1\', port=5000, debug=False)`: Run 
            development server\\n\\n### Blueprint\\n\\n#### `Blueprint(name,    
            import_name, url_prefix=None)`\\n\\nCreate a new blueprint for      
            modular applications.\\n\\n- `name`: Blueprint name\\n-             
            `import_name`: Import name of the blueprint package\\n-             
            `url_prefix`: URL prefix for all blueprint routes\\n\\n####         
            Methods\\n\\n- `route(rule, methods=None, endpoint=None)`: Add route
            to blueprint\\n- `add_url_rule(rule, endpoint, view_func,           
            methods=None)`: Add URL rule to blueprint\\n\\n### Request          
            Object\\n\\nAvailable as the current request in view                
            functions.\\n\\n#### Properties\\n\\n- `method`: HTTP method (GET,  
            POST, etc.)\\n- `path`: Request path\\n- `headers`: Request headers 
            dictionary\\n- `query_string`: Raw query string\\n- `args`: Parsed  
            query parameters\\n- `body`: Request body as bytes\\n- `data`:      
            Request body as string\\n- `form`: Parsed form data (for POST       
