            +app = Flask(__name__)                                              
            +                                                                   
            +@app.route('/hello/<name>')                                        
            +def hello(name):                                                   
            +    return render_template_string('<h1>Hello {{ name }}!</h1>',    
            name=name)                                                          
            +```                                                                
            +                                                                   
            +## Dependencies                                                    
            +                                                                   
            +- **Required:** Python 3.11+                                       
            +- **Optional:** Jinja2 (for template rendering)                    
            +                                                                   
            +## Deployment                                                      
            +                                                                   
            +The framework is fully WSGI-compatible and can be deployed with any
            WSGI server:                                                        
            +                                                                   
            +```bash                                                            
            +# With gunicorn                                                    
            +gunicorn app:app                                                   
            +                                                                   
            +# With uWSGI                                                       
            +uwsgi --http :8000 --wsgi-file app.py --callable app               
            +```                                                                
            +                                                                   
            +## Conclusion                                                      
            +                                                                   
            +The implementation successfully provides all required features:    
            +                                                                   
            +1. ✅ URL routing with variable segments and HTTP method filtering 
            +2. ✅ Request object encapsulating method, path, headers, query    
            string, and body                                                    
            +3. ✅ Response object with status code, headers, and body          
            +4. ✅ Jinja2 template rendering integrated with the application    
            context                                                             
            +5. ✅ Application context management using thread-local storage    
            +6. ✅ Blueprint-based modular applications with URL prefix         
            inheritance                                                         
            +7. ✅ WSGI compliance (verified with wsgiref validator)            
            +8. ✅ Built-in development server                                  
            +                                                                   
            +The framework is production-ready, well-tested, and follows        
            Flask-like conventions while being completely independent and       
            WSGI-compliant.                                                     
